# Real-Time CDC Pipeline: MySQL → Debezium → Kafka → Databricks DLT (Bronze/Silver)
## End-to-End FAANG Interview Guide

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         FULL PIPELINE ARCHITECTURE                              │
│                                                                                 │
│  ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌─────────────┐    ┌───────────────┐  │
│  │   MySQL DB   │    │   Debezium   │    │    Kafka    │    │  Databricks   │  │
│  │              │    │  (Connector) │    │   Cluster   │    │     DLT       │  │
│  │  - binlog    │───▶│  - reads     │───▶│  - Topic:   │───▶│  - Bronze     │  │
│  │    enabled   │    │    binlog    │    │    orders   │    │  - Silver     │  │
│  │  - tables:   │    │  - captures  │    │  - Topic:   │    │  - Autoloader │  │
│  │    orders    │    │    INSERT    │    │    users    │    │  - MERGE INTO │  │
│  │    users     │    │    UPDATE    │    │  - Topic:   │    │  - Quarantine │  │
│  │    products  │    │    DELETE    │    │    products │    └───────────────┘  │
│  └──────────────┘    └──────────────┘    └─────────────┘                       │
│                                                                                 │
│  SOURCE LAYER          CDC LAYER           TRANSPORT          LAKEHOUSE         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Data Flow in Plain English
1. **MySQL** has binary logging (`binlog`) enabled — every INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE is recorded
2. **Debezium** reads that binlog stream, converts each change event into a **structured JSON message**
3. **Kafka** acts as the durable, scalable buffer — one topic per source table
4. **Databricks Structured Streaming** (via DLT) consumes Kafka topics
5. **Bronze layer** — raw CDC events land exactly as received (append-only)
6. **Silver layer** — deduplicated, merged, business-ready records (current state)

