## 5. Schema Evolution Handling

One of the most common real-world issues — source MySQL schema changes must not break the pipeline.

```python
# DLT handles schema evolution via table properties
@dlt.table(
    name="bronze_orders_raw",
    table_properties={
        "delta.columnMapping.mode": "name",  # Name-based column mapping
        "delta.minReaderVersion": "2",
        "delta.minWriterVersion": "5"
    }
)
def bronze_orders_raw():
    return (
        spark.readStream
            .format("kafka")
            ...
            .load()
            # Use schema inference with mergeSchema
            .option("mergeSchema", "true")  # auto-adapt to new columns
    )
```

**How schema changes propagate:**
```
MySQL: ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN discount DOUBLE DEFAULT 0;
  ↓
Debezium: emits new event with discount field
  ↓
Debezium schema-changes topic: records the DDL change
  ↓
Kafka: new messages include discount field
  ↓
Bronze: DLT detects new column → evolves schema automatically (mergeSchema)
  ↓
Silver: APPLY CHANGES INTO applies new column to silver table
```

