## 7. Trade-offs & Design Decisions

### Trade-off 1: Kafka Topic-per-Table vs Single Topic

| | Topic-per-Table | Single Topic |
|---|---|---|
| Parallelism | Independent scaling per table | One consumer group for all |
| Consumer isolation | Yes (DLT stream per topic) | No |
| Backpressure | Isolated per table | One slow table blocks others |
| Operational complexity | More topics to manage | Simpler |
| **Chosen** | **Topic-per-table** | |
| **Reason** | Orders volume is 100x users volume — isolation prevents starvation |

### Trade-off 2: APPLY CHANGES (SCD1) vs SCD Type 2

| | SCD Type 1 | SCD Type 2 |
|---|---|---|
| Storage | Less (only current row) | More (all historical rows) |
| Query simplicity | Simple (no filter needed) | Needs `WHERE is_current=true` |
| Historical analysis | Not possible in silver | Fully supported |
| CDC latency | Lower (simple MERGE) | Higher (insert + expire row) |
| **Chosen** | **SCD Type 1 for silver** | SCD Type 2 for gold (if needed) |
| **Reason** | Silver = current state for dashboards; Gold = history for analytics |

### Trade-off 3: Continuous Streaming vs Triggered Micro-batch

| | Continuous | Triggered (30s interval) |
|---|---|---|
| Latency | Sub-second | 30-60 seconds |
| Cost | High (always-on compute) | Low (scales down between batches) |
| Stability | More complex failure modes | Well-understood checkpointing |
| **Chosen** | **Triggered (30s)** | |
| **Reason** | Business SLA = 2 minutes; 30s satisfies requirement at 70% lower cost |

### Trade-off 4: Kafka JSON vs Avro with Schema Registry

| | JSON | Avro + Schema Registry |
|---|---|---|
| Schema enforcement | None | Strict (fail on schema mismatch) |
| Message size | Larger (verbose) | Smaller (binary) |
| Complexity | Simple | Needs Schema Registry service |
| Evolution safety | Manual | Automatic with compatibility checks |
| **Chosen** | **Avro + Schema Registry** for production | JSON for dev |
| **Reason** | Schema drift is the #1 cause of pipeline failures; enforce at ingest |

